result: 'Lexer already tokenizes `!!`(BangBang) distinct from `!`(Bang). `err <expr>`
  raise parses to Stmt::ErrReturn (parser/stmt/dispatch.rs). Removed the entire `?>`
  propagation mechanism: Token::QuestionGt + its lexing, Expr::Propagate AST node
  and all consumers (typer, resolve, driver/sources/implicit, parser/decl is_value),
  the PendingPropagate struct + pending_propagates field + desugar_propagate + wrap_propagates
  + QuestionGt postfix parsing, and simplified parse_block_items. Updated 2 diagnostic
  strings that mentioned `?>`. Reverted a broken prior-session quaternary WIP in bind.rs
  to the committed baseline so the tree compiles with zero warnings. Pre-marked 7
  `?>`-pinning tests in tests/error_effects.rs #[ignore] with a pointer to task 2-4-7
  for migration. Ternary parsing unaffected. The remaining suite failures are baseline-confirmed
  pre-existing (incomplete `! E`/auto-wrap work) and tracked for 2-4-7.'
description: 'Lexer: tokenize `!!` distinct from `!`. Parser: parse `err <Variant>`
  as a raise statement (distinct from `err <Enum>`+block declaration). Remove `?>`
  (Propagate) parsing + PendingPropagate machinery. Done: err-raise and !! lex/parse
  without breaking ternary.'
